What is derived:

  * The 33 evaluator prompt templates in
    evals4j-core/src/main/java/io/github/grabdoc/evals4j/prompt/Prompts.java
    are reproduced verbatim from openevals/python/openevals/prompts/**.

  * The following algorithms are ports of the corresponding OpenEvals
    implementations, retaining their observable behaviour:
      - the LLM-as-judge output schema construction and score extraction
        (openevals/python/openevals/llm.py)
      - the scorer-to-result normalization contract
        (openevals/python/openevals/utils.py)
      - message normalization and trajectory rendering
        (openevals/python/openevals/utils.py, trajectory/utils.py)
      - trajectory matching in strict/unordered/subset/superset modes and the
        tool-argument matchers (openevals/python/openevals/trajectory/**)
      - structured/JSON match scoring and aggregation
        (openevals/python/openevals/json/match.py)
      - markdown code-block extraction (openevals/python/openevals/code/base.py)
      - the multi-turn simulation loop and simulated user
        (openevals/python/openevals/simulators/**)

